Description: open, private internet speed test for Linux desktops
 Swiftlet measures latency, jitter, download and upload speed with a clean
 Qt desktop interface (it fits the Deepin desktop and works on any Debian
 based distribution) and a command-line mode.
 .
 Tests use the open ndt7 protocol against the public Measurement Lab (M-Lab)
 servers or a self-hosted ndt7 server, or a self-hosted LibreSpeed server.
 Results are kept in a local history that can be exported to CSV.
 .
 Security and privacy: no telemetry, no root, TLS with certificate
 verification for every connection, and network measurements run in a
 separate process sandboxed with Landlock and resource limits.
